      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "\"So I tried creating the config.json in my LocalLow/VRChat/VRChat directory, so my SSD would not get flooded/constantly written to by my cache\"\nWhat an odd reason to even switch the location, if this is concerning to you; you really don't want to find out how much your browser caches data.\nIn any case, make sure you didn't use the JSON escape character \\ and only used / instead as VRChat says, if you must use \\ then use it as \\\\\nMake sure both caches are cleared manually, this doesn't require you to delete every file inside of each cache. Just the folders inside of them like Avatars, Cache-WindowsPlayer, Cookies, Tools, Unity, and VRCHTTPCache then load up VRChat again and see if that helps.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
