  "details": "When the 3.0 Avatars released, and the ability to configure VRChat to assign a different location to store Cache Data was added, I had recently revamped my VR Rig with an SSD+HDD for OS and Storage (respectively; Fresh install of Windows 10, Fresh install of VRChat), So I tried creating the config.json in my LocalLow/VRChat/VRChat directory, so my SSD would not get flooded/constantly written to by my cache. Unfortunately doing this has caused several issues, Everyone's avatar in every world i've loaded into has been showing up with Robots that are labeled Perf-Blocked (My Safety settings are ALWAYS set to None, and trying to change to another setting does NOT fix this) as well as everyone I click on defaults to \"Use Safety Settings\" in the Menu. \nIn addition to this, Any world that i've loaded into with a Twitch Livestream displaying, Does NOT play audio (everyone else can hear the audio) but the Video does display on the screen. \n(P.S. Logging into the VRChat's Canny.io website no longer works with a google account, as it will always come up with an error trying to log in, forcing you to only use your VRChat Account to log in, please fix?)",
